      "widgets_values": [
        "subject_definitions:\n<Subject 1> is the man in <Picture 1>, in his late thirties, with short greying hair, light stubble, a tired but kind face and a navy wool jumper.\n<Subject 2> is the street in <Picture 2>: an empty glass-and-steel bus shelter with a red bench, a lit corner shop with a green awning just behind the shelter, a long row of red-brick terraced houses, warm streetlights and wet tarmac at dusk.\n\nsummary:\n[reference generation] The target video shows <Subject 1> waiting alone at the bus shelter in <Subject 2> at dusk. He looks up the street, checks his watch and mutters about the late bus as the headlights of a passing car sweep across the wet street.\n\nretention_analysis:\n<Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the man's face, short greying hair, light stubble and navy wool jumper are retained.\n<Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - the bus shelter, red bench, corner shop with its green awning, terraced houses, streetlights and wet tarmac are retained.\n\ndetailed_description:\nThe target video is a realistic, live-action cinematic shot at dusk, with cool blue evening light, warm streetlight and a shallow depth of field.\n[Shot 1] A medium shot at eye level frames <Subject 2>, the quiet terraced street just after rain. The glass-and-steel bus shelter with its red bench stands on the left of the frame. Just behind it, the corner shop glows under its green awning, its window full of shelves, and a long row of red-brick terraced houses runs from the shop into the blue evening light. The wet tarmac reflects the warm streetlights in long, broken streaks, and small puddles sit along the kerb. <Subject 1>, the man in his late thirties with short greying hair, light stubble and a navy wool jumper, stands on the wet pavement at the front right corner of the shelter, near the centre of the frame, with his hands in his trouser pockets and his shoulders hunched against the cold. Warm streetlight falls on the left side of his face and the cool sky lights the right. The camera pushes in slowly with small amplitude, moving from a medium shot towards a medium close-up over the length of the shot. He leans forward and looks up the street, squinting into the distance, then straightens with a small sigh that shows faintly as breath in the cold air. He pulls his left hand from his pocket, turns his wrist and checks his watch, then shakes his head with a dry half-smile. <Subject 1> (S1), in a low, calm, slightly husky voice with a soft British accent, says: <d>[English] Ten minutes, it said. Ten minutes.</d> He closes his mouth into a tight, resigned smile, and his lips remain completely closed for the rest of the shot. He puts his hand back in his pocket and looks up the street again, his weight shifting from one foot to the other. Near the end of the shot, a car comes up the street from the distance, its headlights sweeping across the wet tarmac and catching his face and the glass of the shelter in a brief warm glow before moving on. The shop window behind him stays lit and steady, and a few drops of water fall from the edge of the shelter roof onto the pavement beside him. The street stays empty apart from him and the passing car, and the shot ends with him still waiting, looking up the street.\n\noverall_soundscape:\nA quiet evening street: a distant low hum of traffic, water dripping from the shelter roof onto the pavement, the soft scuff of his shoes on wet concrete, a faint electrical buzz from the shop sign, and the rising then fading hiss of tyres on the wet road as the car passes.\n\nnon_diegetic_music:\nN/A"
