      "title": "How to use",
      "properties": {
        "ue_properties": {
          "widget_ue_connectable": {},
          "version": "7.8",
          "input_ue_unconnectable": {}
        }
      },
      "widgets_values": [
        "# h3-r2v-base\n\nMiniMax H3 ref2va: a video with sound, built from reference images of people, places, objects or styles.\n\n## Use\n\n1. **References.** Load images into Picture 1 to 4. The prompt calls them `<Picture 1>` to `<Picture 4>` in the order they are connected. A bypassed loader (Ctrl+B) is skipped and the ones after it move up a number, so fill the slots in order. For more, copy a loader and connect it to the next free `ref_image` input, up to 9. Only the first image of a batch is used.\n2. **Size.** **Size** sets the video's ratio and **Megapixels** its area: 0.98 gives 1344x768 at 16:9, or 768x1344 at 9:16. References keep their own shape. On the reference node, `ref_image_size` `match` scales each reference down to the video's area; `max` keeps up to a 2048 px short edge for closer identity, and the node warns it can be several times slower.\n3. **Prompt.** Six sections in this order, each name on its own line with its text below:\n\n   ```\n   subject_definitions:\n   <Subject 1> is the man in <Picture 1>, with ...\n   <Subject 2> is the room in <Picture 2>: ...\n\n   summary:\n   [reference generation] The target video shows <Subject 1> ... in <Subject 2> ...\n\n   retention_analysis:\n   <Subject 1> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - ...\n   <Subject 2> (appears in [Shot 1]): fully_preserved - ...\n\n   detailed_description:\n   One or two sentences on style.\n   [Shot 1] ...\n   [Shot 2] At 00:03.000, the shot cuts to ...\n\n   overall_soundscape:\n   ...\n\n   non_diegetic_music:\n   N/A\n   ```\n\n   - `<Subject N>` is a person, place, object or style taken from the pictures. Name its source picture in `subject_definitions`, then use only the subject label.\n   - Use `<Picture N>` on its own only when that image is a frame of the video. The summary then starts `[keyframe completion]`, or `[reference generation + keyframe completion]` alongside subjects.\n   - Retention markers: `fully_preserved`, `partially_preserved`, `attribute_transfer`, `weak_reference`.\n   - A speaker is `<Subject 1> (S1)` with the line in `<d>[English] ...</d>`. After the line, describe the mouth closing (\"his lips remain completely closed for the rest of the shot\"), or he may keep talking.\n   - `detailed_description` should be 350 to 500 words.\n4. **Turbo.** On: the ref2v 4-step turbo LoRA (v0.1) at 4 steps, for trying prompts and seeds. Off: 20 steps, for the final. Keep the seed between them.\n5. **LoRAs.** Add your own in the LoRA Manager loader. The turbo LoRA stays outside it, on the Turbo switch.\n\n## Output\n\n`video/<date>/<time>_h3-r2v-base_s<seed>_00001_.mp4`. The workflow, with the Turbo setting, is stored inside each video.\n\nPrompt format: MiniMax's `docs/VIDEO_PROMPT_WRITING_GUIDE_ref_en.md` in MiniMaxAI/MiniMax-H3 on Hugging Face. Notes and timings: gen-ai-docs, `Setup/MiniMax H3 on snug.md`."
      ],
      "color": "#222",
      "bgcolor": "#000"
    },
